            <div xml:id="d812">

                <pb facs="1179" n="1047" xml:id="pg1047"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.74/653: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-01-16T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 16,
                                1926—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received January 16—6:09
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>28. My telegram number 25, January 14, 10 a.m. I am reliably informed that
                    Japanese Minister addressed to the Chinese Government, January 14th, a note
                    protesting against transaction of commercial business with France by French
                    wireless station at Yünnanfu, and with Germany by station at Mukden, reasserting
                    claim to 30-year monopoly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
